From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:28:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Leave the CEC bus when the Linux adapter is closed

The CEC framework of Linux keeps the logical addresses of an adapter
when the file that set them is closed (cec_release(), cec-api.c, only
drops the initiator, the follower and passthrough). Without a follower
it answers for them itself: <Give Physical Address>, <Give Device
Vendor ID>, <Get CEC Version>, and <Feature Abort> to whatever else is
addressed to them (cec_receive_notify(), cec-adap.c); and each time the
physical address comes back (the display or the AV receiver behind the
port turned off and on), it claims them again and broadcasts <Report
Physical Address> and <Device Vendor ID>.

CLinuxCECAdapterCommunication::Close() only closed the file. A client
that closes the adapter while the system goes on - Kodi with its CEC
adapter turned off in its settings - stayed on the bus as a playback
device, answering polls, until the adapter itself went away. Issue #24
of LibreELEC Hades: a TV that changes to the input of an AV receiver on
the DisplayPort CEC (DP-AUX) of the board, and does so "with CEC turned
off as well".

Close() now clears the logical addresses that this handle set, the
unconfigured state that Open() itself starts from, before it closes the
file (logged at NOTICE level, which Kodi's log shows). An adapter that
another program configured and that this handle only probed (Open()
without listening) is left as it is, and so is one whose node is gone
(DeviceGone() already let the file go). Reopening, as Kodi does after a
lost connection or a standby, claims them again as before.

The framework never sends <Active Source>, <Image View On> or a routing
message itself, so this is not the input switch of #24 by any message of
CEC 1.4: what it removes is a closed client that stays on the bus.
libcec 8.1.7 and its master close the file only.
---
 .../Linux/LinuxCECAdapterCommunication.cpp    | 22 ++++++++++++++++++-
 .../Linux/LinuxCECAdapterCommunication.h      |  5 +++++
 2 files changed, 26 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/libcec/adapter/Linux/LinuxCECAdapterCommunication.cpp b/src/libcec/adapter/Linux/LinuxCECAdapterCommunication.cpp
index 61f208e..f7eca06 100644
--- a/src/libcec/adapter/Linux/LinuxCECAdapterCommunication.cpp
+++ b/src/libcec/adapter/Linux/LinuxCECAdapterCommunication.cpp
@@ -73,7 +73,8 @@ static uint32_t GetConfiguredVendorId(IAdapterCommunicationCallback *callback)
 
 CLinuxCECAdapterCommunication::CLinuxCECAdapterCommunication(IAdapterCommunicationCallback *callback, const std::string &strPath /* = "" */)
   : IAdapterCommunication(callback),
-    m_path(strPath)
+    m_path(strPath),
+    m_bLogAddrsSet(false)
 {
   m_fd = INVALID_SOCKET_VALUE;
 }
@@ -217,6 +218,7 @@ bool CLinuxCECAdapterCommunication::Open(uint32_t iTimeoutMs, bool UNUSED(bSkipC
     }
 
     LIB_CEC->AddLog(CEC_LOG_DEBUG, "CLinuxCECAdapterCommunication::Open - ioctl CEC_ADAP_S_LOG_ADDRS - log_addr_mask=%04x num_log_addrs=%u", log_addrs.log_addr_mask, log_addrs.num_log_addrs);
+    m_bLogAddrsSet = true;
 
     if (CreateThread())
       return true;
@@ -233,6 +235,23 @@ void CLinuxCECAdapterCommunication::Close(void)
 
   LIB_CEC->AddLog(CEC_LOG_DEBUG, "CLinuxCECAdapterCommunication::Close - m_fd=%d", m_fd);
 
+  // The CEC framework keeps the logical addresses of an adapter when the file is closed: it goes
+  // on answering for them itself (<Give Physical Address>, <Give Device Vendor ID>, <Get CEC
+  // Version>, <Feature Abort> to the rest), and claims them again, with a <Report Physical
+  // Address> broadcast, each time the physical address comes back. A client that closes the
+  // adapter (Kodi with its CEC adapter turned off) stayed on the bus that way until the adapter
+  // went away. What this handle set is cleared, the unconfigured state Open() starts from; an
+  // adapter that another program set up and this one only probed is left as it is.
+  if (m_fd != INVALID_SOCKET_VALUE && m_bLogAddrsSet)
+  {
+    struct cec_log_addrs log_addrs = {};
+    if (ioctl(m_fd, CEC_ADAP_S_LOG_ADDRS, &log_addrs))
+      LIB_CEC->AddLog(CEC_LOG_WARNING, "CLinuxCECAdapterCommunication::Close - ioctl CEC_ADAP_S_LOG_ADDRS failed - errno=%d: the adapter keeps its logical addresses", errno);
+    else
+      LIB_CEC->AddLog(CEC_LOG_NOTICE, "CLinuxCECAdapterCommunication::Close - the logical addresses are cleared: the adapter leaves the CEC bus");
+  }
+  m_bLogAddrsSet = false;
+
   close(m_fd);
   m_fd = INVALID_SOCKET_VALUE;
 }
@@ -370,6 +389,7 @@ bool CLinuxCECAdapterCommunication::SetLogicalAddresses(const cec_logical_addres
     }
 
     LIB_CEC->AddLog(CEC_LOG_DEBUG, "CLinuxCECAdapterCommunication::SetLogicalAddresses - ioctl CEC_ADAP_S_LOG_ADDRS - log_addr_mask=%04x num_log_addrs=%u", log_addrs.log_addr_mask, log_addrs.num_log_addrs);
+    m_bLogAddrsSet = log_addrs.num_log_addrs > 0;
 
     if (log_addrs.num_log_addrs && !log_addrs.log_addr_mask)
         return false;
diff --git a/src/libcec/adapter/Linux/LinuxCECAdapterCommunication.h b/src/libcec/adapter/Linux/LinuxCECAdapterCommunication.h
index 9be234a..97ff760 100644
--- a/src/libcec/adapter/Linux/LinuxCECAdapterCommunication.h
+++ b/src/libcec/adapter/Linux/LinuxCECAdapterCommunication.h
@@ -127,6 +127,11 @@ namespace CEC
 
     int         m_fd;
     std::string m_path;
+    /*!
+     * @brief This handle set the logical addresses of the adapter (Open(), SetLogicalAddresses()),
+     *        which Close() clears.
+     */
+    bool        m_bLogAddrsSet;
   };
 };
 
